hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"363","Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umayyad narrates, Ubay narrates, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrates, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd Allah bin Zayd, on the authority of his father, said: When we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the morning, I told him about the vision, and he said: “Indeed This vision is true, so stand with Bilal, for he has a softer or longer voice than you, so recite to him what you were told, and he will call out that.” He said: So I did, and when Omar bin Al-Khattab heard Bilal’s call to prayer, he went out to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, dragging his cloak, and he said: Oh Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have seen something like that. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Praise be to God.”"
